course: dictionary
lesson: 7644
title: What is a programmer?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A programmer is a person who writes computer programs. A program is a set of instructions that tells a computer what to do, one step at a time. «Programmers are pattern hunters: if they write the same thing twice, they look for what repeats and what changes.» The clue is the word programmers next to the idea of writing instructions, so a programmer makes the instructions that computers follow.
explain: Read the words around a word to check its meaning. «Big games are made by teams: programmers, artists, designers, writers, sound and music people, testers, producers and more.» The list shows that a programmer is one job in a team, and the games need many jobs to be finished.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A programmer can also be a person who plans programmes for TV or radio. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right. If it is about code or computers, it means the first meaning.
fact: A programmer is a person who writes computer programs.
fact: A program is a set of instructions that tells a computer what to do.
fact: A «computer programmer» writes code for computers.
fact: A «game programmer» makes the code that makes a video game work.
fact: A programmer can also plan programmes for TV or radio.
exercise: What is a programmer? | A person who sells computers in a shop | *A person who writes computer programs | A person who draws pictures for games | A person who plays video games
exercise: According to the text, what do programmers spend more time doing? | Building computers | Writing new code | Watching TV | *Reading code
exercise: «Big games are made by teams.» Which job is not on the list of game team jobs? | *Gardeners | Testers | Writers | Designers
test: What is a «game programmer»? | A person who plays games for a living | A person who sells games in a shop | A person who builds computers | *A programmer who makes video games
test: «Programmers are pattern hunters: they look for what repeats and what changes.» Which word means the same as look for? | *Search | Forget | Ignore | Avoid
exam: Programmers check their code step by step, and «calm, step-by-step checking fixes most bugs»; what does this checking do to bugs? | Makes more of them | *Fixes most of them | Deletes the whole project | Hides them forever
